{"availability":"available","full":"harmyderoman/vuejs-confirm-dialog","name":"vuejs-confirm-dialog","description":"Makes simple to create, reuse, promisify and build chains of modal dialogs in Vue.js","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":59,"forks":8,"created":"2021-12-22T10:46:46Z","updated":"2026-09-25T20:29:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vcd-docs.netlify.app/","topics":["composition-api","dialog","modal","popup","typescript","ui","vue","vuejs"],"demo":"https://vcd-docs.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.436Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.436Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.436Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.436Z","stars":59,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Vue"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Convert your dialogs to async functions and use them all over your project!","This plugin just makes it simple to create, reuse, promisify and build chains of modal dialogs in Vue.js. It provides just one function createConfirmDialog that does all the hard work for you.","How does it work? The idea is simple, this function -- createConfirmDialog gets a modal component and magically provides to it emits confirm and cancel and its props values. This function returns to you a dialog instance that controls the rendering of the modal component and reacts to user decisions. It reduces you to write all the boilerplate code over and over again and makes it simple to reuse your modals everywhere in your project."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/harmyderoman/vuejs-confirm-dialog/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c50c4727e6e69671edeba5e38b90717b27cd4d31fbc6a6045cd0d548b7f347db","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.601Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.601Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Convert your dialogs to async functions and use them all over your project!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/